  "worked_solution": "Since we need to multiply $\\frac{1}{16}$ by $4$, we repeat the fraction model $4$ times, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129500/assets/32c71aa5238d59b9033f86181a7de34674852faf17e1d171ff9c60496bc59169.png)\n\n \n\nThere are $4\\times 1=4$ shaded pieces in total. Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{16}\\times 4=\\frac{4}{16}.\n$$",
